      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "ODESSA Township first settled June 1870, with settlers bringing seed wheat from Russia.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.lakesnwoods.com/Odessa.htm",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A.D. Beardsley founded the village in 1879, also running the depot and general store.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://mnbump.com/city-of-odessa/odessa-history/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The town was platted in 1879 when the railroad extended to that point, becoming a rail hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Odessa%2C_Minnesota",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Beardsley's flour mill burned shortly after World War I, marking a significant early loss for the community.",
